From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:47:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] selftests: apple-dcp: follow the T8132 SuperSpeed host and P3
 paths

The SuperSpeed host start takes the PIPE handler lock with
atcphy_pipehandler_lock_timeout(), adds the t8132_ss, t8132_common_owned
and t8132_failed PHY fields and a T8132 USB3 host configure, and the P3
change lets dwc3_host_exit() see dis_u3_susphy_quirk from the glue's
dt_dis_u3_susphy. The apple-dcp host units extract these functions and
no longer built (19 of 57 units, MEASURED).

Take the harness side of both from the Aurora integration tree: extract
atcphy_pipehandler_lock_timeout() in front of the lock helpers and name it
as the polling caller, give the fixture PHYs the T8132 fields (always
false: the fixtures are older generations, and a T8132 dispatch asserts),
and give the dwc3 fixtures the two SUSPHY fields. No assertion is relaxed.

With it the suite reads 31 ok / 27 not ok on this branch against 27 / 30
on the base: no unit that passes on the base fails here. The 27 that fail
on the base fail for harness drift that predates this series.

[j604: hunks from 4c254113bf (phy.py, lifecycle.py, pm.py, quiesce.py,
 dwc3/mocks.c; its M4 graphics tests and run.py changes not taken) and
 the tools hunks of 9ec757d1fb (dwc3/mocks.c, teardown_pm.py), resolved
 onto the 1.607 harness: this tree's lock list keeps
 atcphy_pipehandler_lock_live, and its fixtures keep their own fields.]

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
